From b3ed32a44f76ac3c78bc5612f205dd215bafdc71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kevin <neonc0in@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 19:40:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Port wlr-layer-shell support (PR #109875) onto
 4.6.1-stable

Rebases MoutonDemocrate's layer-shell implementation from its Aug 2025 master
base onto 4.6.1-stable. Adds zwlr_layer_shell_v1 support so Wayland windows can
be placed on the background/bottom/top/overlay layers, and implements
window_set_mouse_passthrough via wl_surface.set_input_region (previously a stub).

Conflict resolutions:
- servers/display_server.{cpp,h} moved to servers/display/ upstream; retargeted.
- SCsub: kept both xdg_toplevel_icon and wlr_layer_shell protocol generation.
- The PR also deletes DEBUG_LOG_WAYLAND and several unrelated code paths added
  since its base (pointer-frame version fallbacks, keyboard modifier reset on
  unfocus). All such deletions were rejected -- they are incidental to layer
  shell and removing the macro would not compile.
- window_set_size: kept 4.6.1's _update_window_rect path and gave layer surfaces
  an early return through it, so they also get EGL window resize and the rect
  changed callback, which the PR's version skipped.
